# <img src="../../anserini-logo.png" height="30" /> MS MARCO Passage Ranking

**Anserini reproductions from document collection**

+ **Models**: cosDPR-distil with inverted indexes using the "LexLSH" technique (_b_=600) using cached queries
+ **Config**: [`${yaml_short}`](${yaml})
+ **Template**: [`${template_short}`](${template})

This page describes reproductions from the raw document collection using cosDPR-distil on the [MS MARCO passage ranking task](https://github.com/microsoft/MSMARCO-Passage-Ranking), searching inverted indexes using the "LexLSH" technique (_b_=600), as described in the following paper:

> Jimmy Lin and Tommaso Teofili. [Searching Dense Representations with Inverted Indexes.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.01556) arXiv:2312.01556, 2023.

In these experiments, we are using cached queries (i.e., cached results of query encoding).

This page is automatically generated from [this template](${template}) by the `GenerateReproductionDocsFromDocumentCollectionTest` JUnit test case, so do not modify this page directly; modify the template instead.

From one of our Waterloo servers (e.g., `orca`), the following command will perform the complete regression, end to end:

```bash
bin/run.sh io.anserini.reproduce.ReproduceFromDocumentCollection --index --verify --search --config ${test_name}
```

We make available a version of the MS MARCO Passage Corpus that has already been encoded with cosDPR-distil.

From any machine, the following command will download the corpus and perform the complete regression, end to end:

```bash
bin/run.sh io.anserini.reproduce.ReproduceFromDocumentCollection --download --index --verify --search --config ${test_name}
```

The `ReproduceFromDocumentCollection` program automates the following steps, but if you want to perform each step manually, simply copy/paste from the commands below and you'll obtain the same results.

## Corpus Download

Download the corpus and unpack into `collections/`:

```bash
wget ${download_url} -P collections/
tar xvf collections/${corpus}.tar -C collections/
```

To confirm, `${corpus}.tar` is 26 GB and has MD5 checksum `${download_checksum}`.
With the corpus downloaded, the following command will perform the remaining steps below:

```bash
bin/run.sh io.anserini.reproduce.ReproduceFromDocumentCollection --index --verify --search --config ${test_name} \
  --corpus-path collections/${corpus}
```

